@Node coder "(-gONZALEZ & jOE cOOL-)"

 Yes, here we are. We checked this Util on a
 A4000/40 /X 3.37 and
 A4000/40 /X 3.38 Board and never found any bug.
 But if you find one or think this tool could be made
 better so just contact us (Gonzalez & Joe Cool)
 or any other Motion Member.



                           @{" Back to main menu " link "MAIN"}
@endnode
@Node Intro "(-     Features      -)"

 We thought that some boring bbs-addies in the File_Id.Diz 
 should be stripped. So that your Filelist will be 
 complete without any BBS-addy. 
 This tool will clean the File_id.diz before being added 
 in your filelist.
 
 * no Backdoors
 * /3.x only
 
  


                           @{" Back to main menu " link "MAIN"}
@endnode
@Node Install "(-   Installation    -)"

 Extract the whole BBS-Addies Stripper to your RAM.

  /X2.x:    sORRY tHIS dOOR dOESN'T wORK oN /X2.x

  /X3.x: 1) Rename your old Examine.info in Syscmd-Drawer
            to Examin1.info
         2) Copy the 0-Byte Examin1.info from RAM:Commands/BBSCMD/
	    to bbs:Commands/BBSCMD/
         3) Copy then Examin1.info from RAM:COMMANDS/SYSCMD/
            to bbs:Commands/BBSCMD/
         4) Copy sTRIPADDS.rEXX to DOORS:FILEID/
         5) Copy sTRIPADDS.cHECK to DOORS:FILEID/
         6) Copy sTRIPADDS.sTRIP to DOORS:FILEID/

    *** Complete ***

 
                           @{" Back to main menu " link "MAIN"}
@endnode
@Node Instr "(- Instruction -)"

  1)  If you wanna have other Files to be checked you have
      to Edit the sTRIPADDS.cHECK

          cut
   ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
   lha lzh
   LHA x "{#}" FILE_ID.DIZ T: >NIL:
   LHA d "{#}" FILE_ID.DIZ >NIL:
   lha a "{#}" t:FILE_ID.DIZ >NIL:
   txt doc dok dox nfo
   FileIDExtract TxtExtract "{#}" TO T:FILE_ID.DIZ >NIL:
   FileIDExtract TxtDelete "{#}" >nil:
   FileIDExtract TxtAdd "{#}" TEXT T:FILE_ID.DIZ >NIL:
   zip
   UNZIP -x "{#}" FILE_ID.DIZ -d T: >NIL:
   ZIP -d "{#}" FILE_ID.DIZ >NIL:
   ZIP -9 "{#}" t:FILE_ID.DIZ >NIL:
   ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
          cut

   e.g.
   1) lha lzh
   2) LHA x "{#}" FILE_ID.DIZ T: >NIL:
   3) LHA d "{#}" FILE_ID.DIZ >NIL:
   4) lha a "{#}" t:FILE_ID.DIZ >NIL:
   1) The Files  x.lha and y.lzh will be checked
   2) The Command to get the File_Id.Diz
   3) The Command to delete the File_ID.Diz
   4) The Command to save the new File_ID.Diz

  2)  You have to edit your sTRIPADDS.sTRIP

          cut
   ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
   bBS
   Fastest!
   ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
          cut
 
   Now all lines which include this Addys will be deleted



                           @{" Back to main menu " link "MAIN"}
@endnode

